# EdminBoost ANM Compliance

Gate before presenting final code. If any checklist item is "no", fix it first.

See `edminboost-anm-project.mdc`, `edminboost-anm-standards.mdc`, `edminboost-anm-wordpress-php.mdc`.

## Security

- Sanitize on input, escape on output, authorize before action, verify nonce before write.
- Never trust browser or request input.
- Use `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::CAPABILITY` on admin pages and privileged handlers.
- Settings API: `sanitize_callback` via `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Settings::sanitize()`, `show_in_rest => false`.
- AJAX: `EDMINBOOST_ANM_Ajax::verify_request()` — `check_ajax_referer( 'edminboost_anm_admin', 'nonce' )` + capability check. Mirror pattern for new actions.
- Rule export: `admin_post_edminboost_anm_export_rules` — nonce + capability before download.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; prefer Options API (`edminboost_anm_*`) over custom tables.
- Inbox notice HTML: treat as untrusted; use `wp_kses_post()` or equivalent on display; sanitize fields on capture.

## Directory & Privacy

- No obfuscated code, undisclosed telemetry, or hidden external requests.
- No tracking or analytics to vendor servers. Docs link is user-initiated only.
- **Webhook** (`settings.webhook`): disabled by default; user supplies URL; sends notice summary JSON via `wp_remote_post` only when enabled. Document in `readme.txt`.
- **Digest**: uses `wp_mail()` to configured recipients — no third-party email API.
- No spammy readme or deceptive behavior.
- Any new remote integration must be documented, justified, and opt-in.

## Code Quality

- Prefer WordPress core APIs over custom hacks.
- Keep code human-readable for directory review.
- Follow WPCS across PHP, CSS, JS, and HTML.
- Admin-only unless explicitly requested; enqueue plugin-screen assets via `is_plugin_screen()`.
- Interceptor script loads on wp-admin when plugin is enabled — keep payload minimal; no external script URLs.
- Use `edminboost_anm` / `EDMINBOOST_ANM_` prefix consistently.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] No WordPress core modifications
- [ ] GPL-compatible
- [ ] Human-readable, reviewable code
- [ ] User-facing strings translatable (`EDMINBOOST_ANM_TEXT_DOMAIN`)
- [ ] Privileged actions: capability checks (+ nonces for AJAX/admin-post)
- [ ] Input sanitized; output escaped
- [ ] SQL prepared (if any)
- [ ] Assets scoped; admin notices minimal and dismissible
- [ ] Webhook/digest behavior documented; webhook off by default
- [ ] Uninstall path removes plugin data and clears digest cron
- [ ] Unique `EDMINBOOST_ANM_` / `edminboost_anm_` prefix; maintainable structure
- [ ] Would survive WordPress.org review

## Unsafe Requests

If a feature conflicts with the Plugin Handbook, Coding Standards, security best practices, privacy expectations, or Directory Guidelines — refuse the unsafe approach and propose a compliant alternative.
